---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import LegalNav from '../components/LegalNav.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How No Fluff Cruising handles personal information. What we collect, what we do not, and how to reach us." breadcrumbs={[{name:"Privacy", url:"/privacy/"}]}>
  <div class="wrap"><article>
    <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <div class="answer"><b>The short answer</b>If you subscribe, your email goes to beehiiv so we can send the weekly cruise news roundup. We do not invent analytics trackers on this page. Hosting, fonts, video embeds, and the signup form still involve third parties. Email us if you have a privacy question.</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>No Fluff Cruising is operated by Matthew and Marlee. This policy covers nofluffcruising.com.</p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>We do not ask you for an account. If you use the newsletter signup, beehiiv collects the email you submit. If you email us, we receive the address and message you send.</p>

      <h2>Newsletter (beehiiv)</h2>
      <p>Homepage signup embeds a beehiiv subscribe form. The email you enter is processed by beehiiv under their privacy policy. We use it only to send the newsletter you opted into. You can unsubscribe from any issue. Dismissal of the homepage popup is stored in your browser as <code>nfc-nl-dismissed</code> for about 30 days so we do not keep showing it.</p>

      <h2>Hosting</h2>
      <p>The site is hosted on Vercel. Vercel processes standard server logs such as IP address, user agent, and request path as part of delivering the site. See Vercel&rsquo;s own privacy documentation for how that provider handles data.</p>

      <h2>Fonts</h2>
      <p>Pages load fonts from Google Fonts. Your browser contacts Google&rsquo;s servers to fetch those files. Google may process technical data such as IP address under its own policies.</p>

      <h2>YouTube embeds</h2>
      <p>Ship tours and related videos use YouTube nocookie embeds behind a click-to-load facade. Until you click to play, we avoid loading the full player. After you click, YouTube may set cookies and collect data under Google&rsquo;s policies.</p>

      <h2>Outbound partners</h2>
      <p>We link to booking and quote partners, including yourcruisebestie.com and book.cruisesit.com. If you follow those links, those sites handle any information you give them under their own policies. We do not control their forms.</p>

      <h2>Analytics</h2>
      <p>Google Analytics 4 (GA4) loads only when a measurement ID is configured for the site (via the <code>PUBLIC_GA_MEASUREMENT_ID</code> environment variable). When it is set, GA4 may collect standard usage data and campaign or UTM parameters from the URL you arrive with (for example YouTube QR links). When that ID is not configured, we do not load third-party analytics. Newsletter signup still uses beehiiv as described above.</p>

      <h2>How we use email</h2>
      <p>If you contact us, we use your email to reply. We do not sell email lists. We only add you to the newsletter if you opt in through the signup form.</p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>Depending on where you live, you may have rights to access, correct, or delete personal information we hold about you. Email us at the address below to make a request. We will respond within a reasonable time.</p>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>This site is for a general audience and is not directed at children under 13. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child gave us information, contact us and we will delete it.</p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>We may update this policy. The date and text on this page are the current version. Continued use after a change means you accept the updated policy.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Privacy questions: <a href="mailto:portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com">portholesandpixiedust@gmail.com</a>.</p>
    </div>
    <LegalNav />
  </article></div>
</Base>
